    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Kyle Tucker** (69.85), our top two projected producers. **Jackson Merrill** is a priority start, buoyed by a favorable matchup against Sasaki and a 100% stolen base expectation driven by the pitcher's glacial delivery, which aligns perfectly with our organizational mandate to chase speed. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** remains an elite option against Buehler, benefiting from a strong platoon advantage and baseline efficiency that keeps him in the upper echelon despite the park conditions. **Nasim Nunez** (68.24) also earns a high recommendation today; while he occupies the 8-hole, his aggressive base-running profile against a slow delivery makes him a high-leverage play in our quest to win the SB category.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved leaving **Nolan Schanuel** (57.49) on the bench. He posted a respectable score and offered strong plate discipline, but he was ultimately edged out by the superior power-projection and situational matchups of **Coby Mayo** (58.48) and **Curtis Mead** (58.36). While **Nolan Schanuel** offers reliability, the optimizer favored the high-ceiling environments provided for **Curtis Mead** and **Coby Mayo**, both of whom benefit significantly from positive park factors and favorable spots in the batting order. We are keeping a close watch on **Gunnar Henderson** (59.45); despite his raw talent, he faces a significant platoon disadvantage against Alvarez, which suppressed his score. If any late-breaking wind reports materialize, we are prepared to shift our strategy, but for now, the data supports prioritizing high-speed, high-platoon-advantage hitters over raw volume.",
